| Niva Bupa Health Insurance Ltd | 9MFY25 | Investment yield | — | 5.27 | % | Niva Bupa Statutory Results — "Yield on Investments (without unrealized gains)" | https://transactions.nivabupa.com/pages/doc/investor-relations/financial-results/2024-2025/December-31-2024.pdf | 2025-02-04 |

*(Columns for Retail health GWP, PAT-IFRS, Claims ratio, Expense ratio, Commission ratio, Combined ratio, Solvency ratio, Retail health market share, and AUM have been omitted from the table above as these values were not printed anywhere in the fetched pages of the source document — left blank rather than estimated, per instructions.)*

## Sourcing Notes & Key Interpretations

- **GWP basis:** The ₹**4,683.58 crore** GWP figure is on the **1/n statutory basis** — Note 9 of the filing confirms this basis was applied with effect from October 1, 2024, and had already reduced GWP by ₹327.70 crore. This satisfies the "prefer 1/n basis" sourcing rule.
- **NEP derivation:** No single consolidated "Total NEP" line was printed in the document. The **₹3,367.04 crore** figure was derived by summing the three disclosed health-cluster sub-segments (Health + Personal Accident + Travel) in the Annexure-II Segment Reporting — this is a direct sum of disclosed figures, not an estimate.
- **Two EOM ratio variants disclosed:** The document shows two different methodologies:
  - **51.31%** — the formally tabulated "Expense of Management to Net Written Premium Ratio" (reported above, as it matches the requested line-item naming).
  - **39%** (9M-YTD, vs. 37% for Q3 standalone) — an alternate IRDAI EOM-regulation methodology using **gross direct premium** as the denominator instead of net written premium (per Note 5). The two figures differ because of the different denominators, not a discrepancy in underlying expense figures.
- **Investment yield variants:** **5.27%** (without unrealized gains) was reported as the standard yield metric. An alternative **6.09%** (with unrealized gains) is also disclosed in the source but not used in the primary table.

## Additional Context Disclosed in the Source (Not Requested Columns, But Material)

- Gross Direct Premium Growth Rate (9M-YTD): **21.71%**
- Net earning ratio (9M-YTD): **0.20%**
- Operating Profit Ratio (9M-YTD): **2.53%**
- Debt-Equity Ratio: **0.09x**; Current Ratio: **0.20x**; Total Debts to Total Assets: **0.03x**
- Basic & Diluted EPS (9M-YTD): **₹0.04/share**
- Gross NPA: **₹63.24 crore** (0.86% of total investments); Net NPA: **nil**
- **Notable one-off items affecting 9M PAT:**
  - ₹198.37 crore of excess Expenses of Management transferred from the revenue account to the P&L account (Note 5)
  - ₹13.24 crore of IPO-related expenses adjusted against securities premium, with ₹21.53 crore still unadjusted pending invoices (Note 11)
  - A ₹25.00 crore GST payment made under Section 74(5) of the CGST Act pursuant to a DGGI inquiry (Note 7)

## Data Gaps & Recommended Next Steps

A caveat on completeness: the extraction of this 12+ page statutory PDF appears to have skipped front-matter pages containing detailed Gross Direct Premium/EOM tables and, notably, the **Solvency Ratio disclosure block** — the extraction jumps from "Total Expense" directly to the NPA-ratio table, skipping the solvency-margin section that IRDAI mandates in this filing format. As a result, the following were left blank rather than estimated:

- Solvency ratio
- Standalone Claims / Expense / Commission / Combined ratios
- Retail Health GWP breakout
- Assets Under Management (AUM)
- PAT (IFRS basis)
- Retail health market share

**To close these gaps**, I'd recommend either:
1. Re-fetching the same PDF with full-page OCR specifically targeting the skipped solvency-margin section, or
2. Sourcing the company's **"Investor Presentation 9MFY25"** deck (if available), which typically carries the headline Claims/Expense/Combined ratios, Solvency ratio, AUM, and Retail Health market share figures that this statutory NL-format filing does not present in named form — this deck was not among the five URLs provided in this task.</ans>
